<% locals.currentPage = 'utilities'; %>
<%- include('../partials/header') %>

<section class="tk-hero--tight" style="padding-bottom:28px">
  <div class="tk-breadcrumb">// HOME / TOOLBOX / PROJECT TRACKER</div>
  <h1 class="tk-h1" style="font-size:64px">Project tracker.</h1>
  <p class="tk-lede" style="margin-top:12px; max-width:680px">
    Lightweight tracker for projects and their bugs, features, tasks, and notes. Two flavors — pick the one that fits how you work.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="tk-section-tight">
  <div class="tk-2col">
    <div class="tk-card-headed">
      <div class="tk-card-headed__head">
        <span>// FILE-BASED TRACKER</span>
        <span class="yellow">JSON · CHROMIUM</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tk-card-headed__body" style="padding:26px 28px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px">
        <p class="tk-body" style="font-size:15px; margin:0">
          Stores your projects in a single <code class="tk-inline">.json</code> file. Drop the file in Dropbox, OneDrive, or iCloud Drive to keep projects in sync across machines.
        </p>
        <ul style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; font-size:12px; padding-left:18px; color:var(--ink-soft); margin:0">
          <li style="margin-bottom:4px">Best for: multi-machine workflows</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom:4px">Needs Chrome / Edge (File System Access API)</li>
          <li>Download to use fully offline — self-contained HTML</li>
        </ul>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:10px; margin-top:6px">
          <a href="/project-tracker-file.html" class="tk-btn tk-btn--accent" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open →</a>
          <a href="/project-tracker-file.html" class="tk-btn tk-btn--ghost" download="project-tracker-file.html">↓ Download</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tk-card-headed">
      <div class="tk-card-headed__head">
        <span>// BROWSER TRACKER</span>
        <span class="yellow">LOCALSTORAGE · ANY BROWSER</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tk-card-headed__body" style="padding:26px 28px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px">
        <p class="tk-body" style="font-size:15px; margin:0">
          Zero setup — open and start tracking. Your data lives in this browser on this device, and persists between visits.
        </p>
        <ul style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; font-size:12px; padding-left:18px; color:var(--ink-soft); margin:0">
          <li style="margin-bottom:4px">Best for: single-machine, no-fuss tracker</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom:4px">Works in any modern browser</li>
          <li>Tied to this browser — clearing site data erases it</li>
        </ul>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:10px; margin-top:6px">
          <a href="/project-tracker-local.html" class="tk-btn tk-btn--accent" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open →</a>
          <a href="/project-tracker-local.html" class="tk-btn tk-btn--ghost" download="project-tracker-local.html">↓ Download</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================== EXPLAINER ============================== -->
<section class="tk-section">
  <div class="tk-section-head">
    <div class="tk-section-head__n">01</div>
    <div class="tk-section-head__body">
      <div class="tk-section-head__kicker">// How it works</div>
      <h2 class="tk-h2">Two trackers, both on your machine</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tk-section-head__rule"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="tk-prose" style="margin:0">
    <p>
      The project tracker is a single HTML page for keeping projects and the work inside them:
      each project has a status (Planning, In process, QA, Complete) and a list of items typed
      as bugs, new features, tasks or notes, each with a Low, Med or High priority. There is no
      server-side storage: both versions keep your data on your own machine.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>File-based tracker.</strong> Saves everything to one <code>.json</code> file that
      you pick, using the browser's File System Access API, which currently means Chrome or
      Edge on desktop. Put that file in Dropbox, OneDrive or iCloud Drive and the same projects
      follow you between computers. <strong>Browser tracker.</strong> Saves to the browser's
      local storage, works in any modern browser and needs no setup.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Gotcha: local storage is fragile.</strong> The browser tracker's data lives only in
      that browser on that device. Clearing site data or browsing history, or using a private
      window, erases it, and it doesn't sync. If the projects matter, use the file-based
      version, or download the page and keep it with your files.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>When not to use it.</strong> It's built for one person keeping track of their own
      projects. It has no accounts, sharing, comments or notifications, so a team that needs
      those is better served by a hosted issue tracker.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================================ FAQ ================================= -->
